social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Understands general and detailed information, including specialized articles of the professional or academic life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "mental facilities "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the ability to use the brain"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The images are considered to be milestones in the advancement of early man's mental facilities."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le08ob02aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": " These are words you use to talk about civilizations."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "manual dexterity"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the skill of using one's hands to create "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: To paint the images, the artists needed high level manual dexterity."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le08ob02aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "intellectually"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "with intellectual capacity"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adverb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Man was beginning to develop intellectually and master skills that allowed him to show his creativity."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le08ob02aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to master"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to gain a the highest level of skill in a specific area"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Man was beginning to develop intellectually and master skills that allowed him to show his creativity."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le08ob02aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "ochre"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a color made from iron in the earth that can be red or yellow"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Also scattered throughout the caves are stenciled red ochre hand prints."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le08ob02aud05"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Present Perfect Passive to Report Events"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use the passive form of the Present Perfect tense when the action is not done <span class=\"italic\">by</span> the subject but rather <span class=\"italic\">to</span> the subject. Often, it is not known who has done the action."}, {"type": "text", "content": "In articles, stories and academic writing, you often use the passive of the Present Perfect tense. This gives your writing a more sophisticated and dynamic quality. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Look the following examples of an active and passive sentence. Compare their structures."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Active:</br> <span class=\"italic\">Experts have dated prehistoric cave paintings as being done between 40,000 BC and 10,000 BC.</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Passive: </br> <span class=\"italic\">Prehistoric cave paintings have been dated by experts as being done between 40,000 BC and 10,000 BC.</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "As you can see, the structure of the Present Perfect passive is: </br></br> Subject + <span class=\"italic\">has/have</span> <span class=\"italic\">been</span> + past participle"}, {"type": "example", "content": "The cave paintings have been cited as the earliest known art."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Through the cave paintings we have been given an insight into the lifestyle of primitive humans. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Animals have been painted on all of the walls in these caves. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "The animal images in the caves have been done in mainly red and black."}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn10le08ob02re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Present Perfect to Talk About Past Experiences"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use the Present Perfect tense to talk about a past action or an action that began in the past that is connected to the present in some way. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "You can use the Present Perfect tense to talk about experiences. When you use the Present Perfect tense, you think about the past and present together. There is some connection between what happened in the past and now."}, {"type": "text", "content": "For example:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\">I have learned English.</span> = I learned English in the past and now I can speak English. </br><span class=\"italic\">He has bought a  painting.</span> = He bought the painting in the past and now he has a painting."}, {"type": "text", "content": "When you want to refer to an action that recently happened, you use the word <span class=\"italic\">just.</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "For example:</br><span class=\"italic\">I have <span class=\"strong\">just</span> started the car.</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "When you want to talk emphasize that an action started and is ongoing at the present time, you use the word <span class=\"italic\">already.</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "For example:  </br><span class=\"italic\">I have <span class=\"strong\">already</span> started the car.</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "When you ask questions using the Present Perfect, you often use words like <span class=\"italic\">ever</span> and<span class=\"italic\"> yet</span>."}, {"type": "text", "content": "For example: </br><span class=\"italic\">Have these types of discoveries <span class=\"strong\">ever</span> come to light any way but by accident?</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "You use <span class=\"italic\">never</span> in negative statements,</br></br>  For example: </br><span class=\"italic\"> I have <span class=\"strong\">never</span> been into a prehistoric cave, but I have wanted to visit one.</span>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "I have read several account of how someone had just come across an opening and wandered in to find 35,000 year ."}, {"type": "example", "content": "They have already been documented in France, Spain, Romania and Sulawesi. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Many in Africa have not be fully explored yet."}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I find out about the caves at Lascaux or Chauvet."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I make notes on the art."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I  prepare a short talk on the paintings."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I use the Present Perfect and the Present Perfect Passive."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I present my talk to a partner or small group."}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Go online or to the library to find out about the caves at Lascaux or Chauvet."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Look at the pictures and read about the animals and hand prints that have been documented."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Make notes on what you read and see."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Prepare a short talk on what you have discovered about the cave paintings."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Present your short talk to another student or a group."}]}], "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"_data": [], "template_override": 1, "type": "welcome", "contents": [{}], "id": 0}, {"id": 1, "type": "audio", "title": "", "_data": [], "template_override": 1, "contents": [{"type": "slideshow", "value": {"audiosrc": "engenn10le08ob02re2aud01", "coverimg": "engenn10le08ob02re2img01.jpg", "images": [{"text": "", "id": 0, "time": "0", "image": "engenn10le08ob02re2img01.jpg"}, {"text": "I have never been into a prehistoric cave, but I have wanted to visit one. Have these types of discoveries ever come to light any way but by accident? Probably not.</br></br>I have read several accounts of how someone has just come across an opening and wandered in to find 35,000- year-old pictures. They have already been documented in France, Spain, Romania and Sulawasi. Many in Africa have not be fully explored yet.", "id": 1, "time": "100", "image": "engenn10le08ob02re2img01.jpg"}, {"text": "The cave paintings have been cited as the earliest known art. They have been dated by experts as  being done between 40,000 BC and 10,000 BC, during the Old Stone Age period.\nThrough the cave paintings we have been given an insight into the lifestyle of primitive humans.\n</br></br>\nAnimals have been painted on all of the walls in these caves. The obvious importance of animals in the lives of early man can be seen from this. However, the depictions have given us a far better understanding.\n</br></br>\nThe images are considered to be milestones in the advancement of early man's mental facilities. Furthermore, the artists needed high level manual dexterity. Man was beginning to develop intellectually and master skills that allowed him to show his creativity.", "id": 2, "time": "29000", "image": "engenn10le08ob02re2img02.jpg"}, {"text": "The animal images in the caves have been done in mainly red and black.  Although many animals pictured on the walls were hunted by the primitive man, others were not. So they cannot all be tied to hunting ritual.\n</br></br>\nAlso scattered throughout the caves are stenciled red ochre hand prints. What is most interesting is the fact that even though these artists clearly had the capacity to depict humans, they chose not to.", "id": 3, "time": "77000", "image": "engenn10le08ob02re2img03.jpg"}]}}]}], "exercises": [{"questions": [], "stimuli_ids": [0], "id": 0, "type": "WLC", "img_path": "", "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can talk about history and civilization."}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can report facts about events or actions."}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can talk about unusual events in the past. "}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": " What was your country like 35,000 years ago?"}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": " What do you know about prehistoric art?"}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": " What animals do you think they painted?"}]}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"type": "group_name", "content": "Welcome"}]}, {"type": "feedback", "content": {"allowed_attempts": 2, "correct_feedback": "Correct", "attempt_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "You have 2 tries"}, {"type": "text", "content": "you have 1 attempt left"}], "incorrect_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "try again"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Maybe next time"}]}}, {"type": "free_header_text", "content": " Ask your partner:"}, {"type": "free_type_text_area", "content": " Look at the picture of prehistoric cave paintings!"}], "template_override": 1}, {"questions": [{"_data": [{"type": "question", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}]}], "id": 0, "responses": [{"correct": 0, "_data": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}], "selected": 0, "id": 0}, {"correct": 1, "_data": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}], "selected": 0, "id": 1}]}], "stimuli_ids": [1], "id": 1, "type": "STI", "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"type": "text", "conte